cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the GICQI metric, please cite the paper below."
title: "GISR-Net: An image-to-scalar regressor for quality assessment of illumination correction in dermatological macro-photographs"
abstract: >-
  GISR-Net is a GoogLeNet-based image-to-scalar regressor that predicts the
  quality of illumination-corrected dermatological macro-photographs. It is
  trained with task-based supervision: the target is the mean Dice similarity
  index obtained by Otsu, minimum error and Kapur maximum entropy thresholding,
  so the predicted score (the GoogLeNet Illumination Correction Quality Index,
  GICQI) agrees with downstream lesion-segmentation accuracy rather than with
  subjective perceptual quality. All results are obtained under
  source-image-disjoint six-fold cross-validation.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/VipinBioLab/GISR-Net"
keywords:
  - no-reference image quality assessment
  - task-based image quality assessment
  - illumination correction
  - dermatological macro-photographs
  - skin lesion segmentation
  - image-to-scalar regression
  - deep learning

